1
00:00:00,176 --> 00:00:08,570
(Q11（Matching）) [志愿服务] Good morning everyone.I’m Steve Wainwright, from Elmleigh Town Council, and I organise the town’s volunteer scheme.

2
00:00:08,570 --> 00:00:12,586
I’m delighted you’re all interested in joining the scheme.

3
00:00:12,586 --> 00:00:24,556
Our volunteers help to create a sense of community among the many people who live in our historic town of Elmleigh, and make residents and visitors feel welcome at local events.

4
00:00:24,556 --> 00:00:30,612
First I’ll mention just a few of the activities that volunteers carry out.

5
00:00:30,612 --> 00:00:36,501
One is to walk around the town centre streets wearing our volunteer T-shirt.

6
00:00:36,501 --> 00:00:44,975
Tourists often ask how to get to a particular shop, and they might also be grateful for recommendations about what to visit.

7
00:00:44,975 --> 00:00:56,632
[活动引导] The town holds a large number of concerts each year, and part of the volunteers’ role is to get everyone in the audience to the right place as smoothly as possible.

8
00:00:56,632 --> 00:01:03,864
You’d be surprised how many people buy tickets then don’t check them, and head for the wrong section of the hall!

9
00:01:03,864 --> 00:01:11,821
Volunteers may get involved with community groups, such as sports clubs or gardeners’ associations.

10
00:01:11,821 --> 00:01:16,555
Here the volunteers talk about how groups can help each other.

11
00:01:16,555 --> 00:01:28,977
For instance, a writing group might want to travel to another town to hear a talk by a well-known author, but may not know that another club has a coach they could travel in.

12
00:01:28,977 --> 00:01:35,924
[居民交流] The town produces a monthly magazine, and anyone who lives in the town can send in articles.

13
00:01:35,924 --> 00:01:44,521
It’s free to residents, and is paid for by local businesses – that’s the responsibility of the council’s advertising department.

14
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:54,078
We depend on volunteers, though, to find out what people think of events they’ve attended, and any suggestions they have for the future.

15
00:01:54,078 --> 00:01:57,665
The volunteers then send a summary to the editors.

16
00:01:57,665 --> 00:02:06,669
There are a number of clubs for retired people, and every year, the council arranges lunch for all the members.

17
00:02:06,669 --> 00:02:18,946
The volunteers welcome the guests, and when everyone’s sitting down and relaxing after the meal, some volunteers put on a show – usually around half an hour of songs and short plays.

18
00:02:18,946 --> 00:02:24,269
The club members really welcome the chance to chat to the volunteers at these events.

19
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:32,597
The town council has a website, of course, and volunteers are asked to help by making sure residents know about it.

20
00:02:32,597 --> 00:02:40,526
It’s updated every day with information about future activities, and we want as many people as possible to use it.

21
00:02:40,526 --> 00:02:47,737
(Q17（单选）) OK, now you know some of the things our volunteers do, I’ll go on to some practical matters.

22
00:02:47,737 --> 00:02:56,763
As you probably know, the town arranges three major festivals every year, and they all depend on a large number of volunteers.

23
00:02:56,763 --> 00:03:02,943
[Q17干扰项C： 未提及志愿者数量] The book festival lasts three days, and uses several venues, which all need volunteers.

24
00:03:02,943 --> 00:03:12,759
[Q17答案句B+Q17干扰项A：     A：more， B：even more = largest number 三个里面最多] More are needed for the music festival, because that lasts a whole week, and even more help is required for the science festival, even though it’s only two days long.

25
00:03:12,759 --> 00:03:15,940
It involves quite a lot of venues, though.

26
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:23,724
(Q18) [Q18干扰项B 仅提及 不符合most] It’s a good idea to help at the festival you’re most interested in, because you can attend most of the events for free.

27
00:03:23,724 --> 00:03:38,664
[Q18干扰项C，仅提及 不符合most限定] We try to use volunteers who are flexible, though, because some festival events are held outdoors, and the weather may affect the size of the audience, and even whether the event can take place; so there can be changes at short notice.

28
00:03:38,664 --> 00:03:50,228
[Q18答案句（A） essential = most important] What’s essential, though, is being able to get on well with other people, and also to deal with someone who’s behaving badly – as occasionally happens.

29
00:03:50,228 --> 00:03:57,601
(Q19) [Q19干扰项A： 主体不符，不是training] Our plan is to get you all working in September, after a week’s training starting on the 2nd.

30
00:03:57,601 --> 00:04:02,950
[Q19答案句B： timetable ... for duties = work 解释， from ... onward 从…开始= begin] So we’ll be timetabling you for duties the following week, from the 9th onward.

31
00:04:02,950 --> 00:04:14,139
[Q19干扰项C： chat,不符合 题干work] Later, in the week beginning September 23rd, we have a chat with each of you, to find out how you feel about being a volunteer, and what extra support you need.

32
00:04:14,139 --> 00:04:19,103
(Q20) As a thank you to the volunteers, we arrange an annual event.

33
00:04:19,103 --> 00:04:26,877
[Q20干扰项C/干扰项B。 C： have had ,过去。    B： 排除依据 不符合时间限定：  last year] In recent years we’ve had a party in the town hall, and last year a barbecue in Chamber Park.

34
00:04:26,877 --> 00:04:32,402
[Q20答案句A： forthcoming = next ,    trip along the canal = boat trip] Our forthcoming event is a trip along the canal from here to Dewhurst and back.

35
00:04:32,402 --> 00:04:38,946
It’s on Saturday September the 28th, and if you’d like to attend, you can sign up once you start work.

36
00:04:38,946 --> 00:04:41,446
Now this is the volunteers’ T-shirt …

